  Memoize is a fast and flexible package for externalization of typesetting
  results, and for memoization of compilation results in general.  By allowing
  the author to reuse the results of compilation of computationally intensive
  pieces of the document, it can radically cut down the compilation time of
  successive compilations.

  In this article I introduce externalization and memoization, outline
  how they are implemented in Memoize, show how to use the package, and
  shamelessly try to entice package writers to support it in their packages.
